      "text": "To find the area of a triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle using the base and height. The base of the triangle is the horizontal distance between \\((0,0)\\) and \\((7,0)\\), which is 7 units. The height of the triangle is the vertical distance from \\((0,0)\\) to the line passing through \\((0,5)\\) and \\((7,12)\\). We can find this height by using the formula for the distance between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\), which is \\(\\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\\).\n\n1. Calculate the length of the base.\n2. Calculate the height of the triangle using the coordinates of the points.\n3. Use the height to find the area of the triangle.\n\nLet's execute these steps in Python to ensure the accuracy of our result.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Coordinates of the vertices\nx1, y1 = 0, 0\nx2, y2 = 7, 0\nx3, y3 = 0, 5\nx4, y4 = 7, 12\n\n# Calculate the length of the base\nbase_length = abs(x1 - x2)\n\n# Calculate the height\nheight = abs(y3 - y1)  # or abs(y2 - y4) depending on which base we use\n\n# Calculate the area using base and height\narea = (base_length * height) / 2\n\n# Round the result to the nearest tenth\narea_rounded = round(area, 1)\nprint(area_rounded)\n```\n```output\n17.5\n```\nThe area of the triangle with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\) is \\(\\boxed{17.5}\\) square units.",
